{"version": 2, "width": 110, "height": 42, "timestamp": 1791880927, "idle_time_limit": 2.0, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/bash", "TERM": "screen"}, "title": "MPI on 16 Blackhole X280 cores"}
[0.015097, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[J"]
[0.016328, "o", "\u001b[1m16 MPI ranks on the 16 X280 cores of one Tenstorrent Blackhole\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m# Blackhole has 4 L2CPU tiles x 4 SiFive X280 cores. Each tile is a coherent\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m# 4-core cluster with its own CLINT and L3; coherence stops at the tile boundary.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m# So: one Linux guest per tile, and MPI across the four guests.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33m## 1. Boot Linux on all four L2CPU tiles (one chip reset)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
